From 253d2a59016c0a9b8b3114022bef95fbf7343eed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jojo2357 <11406210-jojo2357@users.noreply.gitlab.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:12:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] performance_page: Fix sidebar ordering and visibility

Make position and visibility functions of GSettings that GTK evaluates
through a sort function and a filter function, so rows can come and go
freely.

This means that the names of devices that are not present are kept,
which in turn lets an unplugged device, or one that is known but not
yet enumerated, reclaim its position.

A device seen for the first time is merged in after the last device
that sorts before it by default, and the merged order is stored.

Closes #256, #461, #539, and #540

See merge request mission-center-devs/mission-center!538
